1
00:00:00,836 --> 00:00:02,663
Rain on a Saturday empties the shop.

2
00:00:04,010 --> 00:00:06,541
A home game could crowd the
street, or it might not.

3
00:00:08,237 --> 00:00:12,230
Either way, as an owner, your week swings,
and you can't plan around it.

4
00:00:14,204 --> 00:00:18,141
Offset is built on four principles.
Measured, not guessed.

5
00:00:18,141 --> 00:00:22,079
Built for steady income.
The owner's call, every time.

6
00:00:22,079 --> 00:00:23,391
And interpretable, human-facing.

7
00:00:24,959 --> 00:00:28,334
Offset measures that swing in real
dollars, from your own revenue.

8
00:00:29,584 --> 00:00:32,875
It finds a Kalshi contract that
pays out when that risk hits.

9
00:00:32,875 --> 00:00:33,698
And you decide.

10
00:00:35,375 --> 00:00:38,459
Here's a bike shop with
fictional sales but real weather.

11
00:00:38,459 --> 00:00:39,692
Upload its daily revenue.

12
00:00:41,802 --> 00:00:46,718
Rain costs it nearly $2,000 a day, and
that holds up on data the model never saw.

13
00:00:48,457 --> 00:00:50,452
Knicks games? No real effect.

14
00:00:50,452 --> 00:00:56,039
In our research we tested about forty
risks like this, and most were noise.

15
00:00:56,039 --> 00:01:00,429
And a fake effect we planted
lands inside the model's range,

16
00:01:00,429 --> 00:01:02,424
so the test is reliable.

17
00:01:02,734 --> 00:01:05,555
The desk picks Kalshi's rain
contract for Central Park,

18
00:01:05,555 --> 00:01:07,749
the same weather station we measured with.

19
00:01:09,738 --> 00:01:12,754
It buys only enough contracts
to cover the measured loss,

20
00:01:12,754 --> 00:01:15,770
and not more, and shows
the full cost up front.

21
00:01:17,917 --> 00:01:20,277
But not every risk gets a hedge.

22
00:01:20,277 --> 00:01:24,323
For a taxi fleet, rain looked big
last year, then almost vanished.

23
00:01:24,323 --> 00:01:26,683
So Offset says no, and explains why.

24
00:01:28,868 --> 00:01:30,934
And nothing happens
until the owner approves.

25
00:01:33,398 --> 00:01:36,805
Every proposal, decline and
approval is logged with its reasons.

26
00:01:39,882 --> 00:01:43,080
Approved hedges go into the books,
and Offset even caught

27
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:47,877
a deposit that came in eighty-nine cents
short, and named the fee as the cause.

28
00:01:49,834 --> 00:01:52,760
Offset. Steady income in an unsteady week.

